If P has a form that contains <i>, and if the type of i differs from the type of the corresponding template parameter of the template named by the enclosing simple-template-id, deduction fails. If P has a form that contains [i], and if the type of i is not an integral type, deduction fails. If P has a form that includes noexcept(i) and the type of i is not bool, deduction fails. [Example 13:

