Required behavior: Return a non-null pointer to suitably aligned storage ([basic.stc.dynamic]), or else throw a bad_alloc exception. This requirement is binding on any replacement versions of these functions.

[[nodiscard]] void* operator new(std::size_t size);
[[nodiscard]] void* operator new(std::size_t size, std::align_val_t alignment);

Default behavior: Executes a loop: Within the loop, the function first attempts to allocate the requested storage. Whether the attempt involves a call to the C standard library functions malloc or aligned_alloc is unspecified. Returns a pointer to the allocated storage if the attempt is successful. Otherwise, if the current new_handler ([get.new.handler]) is a null pointer value, throws bad_alloc. Otherwise, the function calls the current new_handler function. If the called function returns, the loop repeats. The loop terminates when an attempt to allocate the requested storage is successful or when a called new_handler function does not return.

