A specialization for array types is provided with a slightly altered interface. Conversions between different types of unique_ptr<T[], D> that would be disallowed for the corresponding pointer-to-array types, and conversions to or from the non-array forms of unique_ptr, produce an ill-formed program. Pointers to types derived from T are rejected by the constructors, and by reset. The observers operator* and operator-> are not provided. The indexing observer operator[] is provided. The default deleter will call delete[].

