Class template generator presents a view of the elements yielded by the evaluation of a coroutine.

A generator generates a sequence of elements by repeatedly resuming the coroutine from which it was returned. Elements of the sequence are produced by the coroutine each time a co_yield statement is evaluated. When the co_yield statement is of the form co_yield elements_of(r), each element of the range r is successively produced as an element of the sequence. [Example 1:

generator<int> ints(int start = 0) {
 while (true)
 co_yield start++;
}
void f() {
 for (auto i : ints() | views::take(3))
 cout << i << ' '; // prints 0 1 2
}

— end example]

