Effects: Sets the values of X−r,…,X−1, in that order, as specified below. If X−1 is then 0, sets c to 1; otherwise sets c to 0.To set the values Xk, first construct e, a linear_congruential_engine object, as if by the following definition:

linear_congruential_engine<result_type,
 40014u,0u,2147483563u> e(value == 0u ? default_seed : value);

Then, to set each Xk, obtain new values z0,…,zn−1 from n=⌈w/32⌉ successive invocations of e. Set Xk to (∑n−1j=0zj⋅232j)modm.

