Class ctype encapsulates the C library <cctype> features. istream members are required to use ctype<> for character classing during input parsing.

The specializations required in Table 104 ([locale.category]), namely ctype<char> and ctype<wchar_t>, implement character classing appropriate to the implementation's native character set.

