Returns: do_hash(low, high).

int do_compare(const charT* low1, const charT* high1,
 const charT* low2, const charT* high2) const;

Returns: 1 if the first string is greater than the second, -1 if less, zero otherwise. The specializations required in Table 104 ([locale.category]), namely collate<char> and collate<wchar_t>, implement a lexicographical comparison ([alg.lex.comparison]).

